1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:06,040
In Palestine, Israel has thus far been highly successful in forcibly establishing itself

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:12,720
both as a colonial reality and as a powerful nation-state in a post-colonial age.

3
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:17,380
It has done this while always assuming a false posture of self-defense,

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,860
which I'm sure will be familiar to most of you.

5
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:25,460
The great historian and theoretician of colonialism, Patrick Wolfe,

6
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,660
who sadly just passed away, wrote the following.

7
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:30,520
I'm quoting Patrick Wolfe.

8
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:39,080
Settler colonies were, in brackets, are, premised on the elimination of the native societies.

9
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:48,800
The split tensing were, are, the split tensing reflects a determinate feature of settler colonization.

10
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:52,200
The colonizers come to stay.

11
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:56,700
Invasion is a structure, not an event.

12
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,700
He's thinking, of course, of Australia.

13
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,520
You could say the same thing about New Zealand.

14
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:04,440
You could say the same thing about Canada or the United States.

15
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:07,020
But think of those words in regard to Palestine.

16
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:14,640
In Palestine, both that structure and the war that resulted from it are still ongoing today, after 100 years.

17
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:18,820
It is a war that seems endless to the Palestinians themselves.

